    "body": "> When revisiting a decision, please find the relevant changes & issues. It does seem that from a quick skim of [w3c/csswg-drafts#10857](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10857) and [w3c/csswg-drafts#10908](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10908) there's very few hits for `counter`.\n\nYeah I tried. I looked back at https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10857 including the history in OP but the original message included the `fake-counter-name` concept.\n\n> But after a little bit more searching I stumbled upon [w3c/csswg-drafts#10380 (comment)](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10380#issuecomment-2189394753) which explains it exactly.\n\nThanks for digging this out. \n\n> It's unclear to me if either of your proposals work across writing modes. 1 seems like it won't. 2 maybe? I'm not sure what 2 is exactly.\n\nYeah I think you're right - 1 won't work with writing modes. 2 would as it would still reference the counter style.",
