    "updated_at": "2026-06-09T17:33:39Z",
    "body": "My understanding is that a use of a counter name in generated content doesn't cause any changes to the scoping or numbering of that named counter.  (I admit it's been [over 2 decades](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3247#c100) since I really worked closely on counters, though.)  So use of a counter name should be side-effect-free, with the possible exception of performance.  And even for performance, implementations probably ought to optimize `counter()` (though not `counters()`!) functions whose list style type is one of the [5 simple symbolic counter styles](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-counter-styles-3/#simple-symbolic) to avoid having any interaction with counter numbering at all.\n\nSo I think the use of the name in this context doesn't actually expose that name in any way with the possible exception of performance effects that *ought* to be optimized away.  Or is that not the case for some reason I've forgotten?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
